{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf","id":437362,"title":"How Do You Kill a Werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T12:49:01-07:00","id":437362,"title":"How Do You Kill a Werewolf?","content":"So, I don't know if this has come up yet. <br /> <br /> I mainly run werewolf games, rather than play in them, and it has influenced my perception of the game a great deal. Instead of getting overly excited about big changes, I am very cautious as I understand how much I have to know, and understand, to still tell compelling and challenging stories. <br /> <br /> One of my concerns is the healing factor of Gauru form in the new rule set. <br /> <br /> As the form heals all lethal and bashing at the beginning of each turn, I can see it becoming very difficult to hurt a character with 12 health levels, as even two or three monstrous creatures attacking it are going to come out to around 10 or 12 lethal, which then heals completely. That of course, is giving the attackers a lot of credit considering the higher defense in God Machine, the defense vs firearms and bows, and armor (which I think Gauru still has? It's on the character sheet, but not in the book as far as I or my colleague Handriel can tell.)<br /> <br /> I think this is a powerful and exciting edition that could lead to some truly climatic fights. However, once the short Gauru duration wears out, the character to go into Basu-Im and basically keep the form indefinitely in a combat barring some serious running (which is hard, as Gauru are fast, and the new Father Wolf Speed Strength Gift activates for free in Basu-Im). <br /> <br /> So let me postulate three scenarios, and let me know what you think, because I have trepidations that my foes that I create will be little more than speed bumps unless they are earth-shatteringly powerful: <br /> <br /> 1. Werewolf on Werewolf action (not the sexy kind) - I have two werewolves fighting. One goes to Gauru, then deathrages. This pulls the other into Deathrage. They are now beating on one another. I don't see a 'fox frenzy' anymore, and so do the two just wail on one another until someones Basu-Im timer clicks out, and dies horrifically?<br /> <br /> 2. Werewolf on anything that doesn't do aggravated - I understand that the harrying phase, werewolves actually heal less now than before, but once the Gauru kicks out, things go nuts. My issue here, is if things ever go sour, the werewolf hits the big red button and kills everything. How does an Azlu or beshilu pose a combative threat? Are in oWod with aggravated all day, because nothing else save dropping a building on the werewolf will even slow them down? <br /> <br /> 3. Aggravated: So using silver does the trick. Is the system really pushing for more aggravated to be present? I find that kind of disturbing if its the case, but perhaps I'm still locked in 1.0, where you learn 'aggravated is no no'. I guess the idea of having more things do aggravated kind of unnerves me. In addition, I believe it mentions that werewolves do not take aggravated from anything mundane anymore, only supernatural and silver. Is this the case? I have another question about dealing aggravated, but I'll make a separate topic for it. <br /> <br /> I like to run encounters that involve investigation and social antics, and lead up to combats, same as everyone else. I want to make those combats hard pressed and the victory leaving the players thinking DAMN. Reading the book, unless I'm dealing with other Uratha, I get the feeling the end results is Gauru popping noises and switching to Down and Dirty, because, might as well. <br /> <br /> Could I get some help? I've been thinking about this a lot, and can't wrap my brain around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:10:30-07:00","id":437429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf#post437362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I don't know if this has come up yet.<br /> <br /> I mainly run werewolf games, rather than play in them, and it has influenced my perception of the game a great deal. Instead of getting overly excited about big changes, I am very cautious as I understand how much I have to know, and understand, to still tell compelling and challenging stories.<br /> <br /> One of my concerns is the healing factor of Gauru form in the new rule set.<br /> <br /> As the form heals all lethal and bashing at the beginning of each turn, I can see it becoming very difficult to hurt a character with 12 health levels, as even two or three monstrous creatures attacking it are going to come out to around 10 or 12 lethal, which then heals completely. That of course, is giving the attackers a lot of credit considering the higher defense in God Machine, the defense vs firearms and bows, and armor (which I think Gauru still has? It's on the character sheet, but not in the book as far as I or my colleague Handriel can tell.)<br /> <br /> I think this is a powerful and exciting edition that could lead to some truly climatic fights. However, once the short Gauru duration wears out, the character to go into Basu-Im and basically keep the form indefinitely in a combat barring some serious running (which is hard, as Gauru are fast, and the new Father Wolf Speed Strength Gift activates for free in Basu-Im).</div> </div> </div> </div>The healing factor and additional health levels of Gauru didn't stop two Uratha being killed in two rounds in one of my playtest games, one of whom was a Rahu with a focus on Stamina in Gauru <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No-one in that fight had access to Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So let me postulate three scenarios, and let me know what you think, because I have trepidations that my foes that I create will be little more than speed bumps unless they are earth-shatteringly powerful:<br /> <br /> 1. Werewolf on Werewolf action (not the sexy kind) - I have two werewolves fighting. One goes to Gauru, then deathrages. This pulls the other into Deathrage. They are now beating on one another. I don't see a 'fox frenzy' anymore, and so do the two just wail on one another until someones Basu-Im timer clicks out, and dies horrifically? </div> </div> </div>Ok, so what <i>should</i> be in the death rage rules (haven't received my comp copy yet, still working off the drafts, but I am assuming it's still in since it's rather important: <i>Death raging Uratha do not treat other death raging Uratha as targets</i>. The two death ragers will now start <i>killing everything else</i> nearby.<br /> <br /> [quote[2. Werewolf on anything that doesn't do aggravated - I understand that the harrying phase, werewolves actually heal less now than before, but once the Gauru kicks out, things go nuts. My issue here, is if things ever go sour, the werewolf hits the big red button and kills everything. How does an Azlu or beshilu pose a combative threat? Are in oWod with aggravated all day, because nothing else save dropping a building on the werewolf will even slow them down?[/quote]<br /> <br /> There are all sorts of tricks to deal with Gauru. Numbers and focused fire will kill quite effectively. Using tilts and crippling effects, the environment and other factors to weaken and obstruct a Gauru all work fine. Taking advantage of a Gauru's more limited capability to do anything other than killing can work well, luring or baiting the Gauru away or just keeping it chasing until it burns through its war form time.<br /> <br /> Gauru is terrifying; many of the werewolves' enemies are aware of that, and use tactics to compensate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Aggravated: So using silver does the trick. Is the system really pushing for more aggravated to be present? I find that kind of disturbing if its the case, but perhaps I'm still locked in 1.0, where you learn 'aggravated is no no'. I guess the idea of having more things do aggravated kind of unnerves me. In addition, I believe it mentions that werewolves do not take aggravated from anything mundane anymore, only supernatural and silver. Is this the case? I have another question about dealing aggravated, but I'll make a separate topic for it. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf 2nd edition actually has <i>less</i> Aggravated damage access than the 1st edition.<br /> <br /> When it refers to mundane things not doing Aggravated damage, it <i>doesn't</i> mean mundane damage that has done so many levels of Lethal or Bashing that they've wrapped round to Aggravated; just to mundane forms of damage that usually deal Aggravated damage by default (although I don't think there are many such sources).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like to run encounters that involve investigation and social antics, and lead up to combats, same as everyone else. I want to make those combats hard pressed and the victory leaving the players thinking DAMN. Reading the book, unless I'm dealing with other Uratha, I get the feeling the end results is Gauru popping noises and switching to Down and Dirty, because, might as well.<br /> <br /> Could I get some help? I've been thinking about this a lot, and can't wrap my brain around it. </div> </div> </div>Would it help to give some combat examples and scenarios?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:14:42-07:00","id":437432,"title":"","content":"1. With your two werewolves, the other one wouldn't be pulled into death rage unless they were a packmate of the first. The first wouldn't necessarily death rage unless they were in the form for too long. From there, if one of the werewolves is physically superior, they may win the battle. If either have packmates, they would likely turn the tide. Otherwise if your werewolves are merely standing there trading punch for punch, it's possible they'll end up in a stalemate, and maybe next time one of them will try harder.<br /> <br /> 2. The healing works per turn, like at the beginning of theirs. Providing there are multiple enemies, it's entirely possible, and even likely, that they'll manage to push things over into aggravated damage, especially since your scenarios rely on an individual werewolf without combat ability. Plus azlu and beshilu can get really big. Just looking at some of their options for Dread Powers in the book, you can see something like Toxic Bite, which can cause penalties to all actions through the Sickness tilt, or damage through the Poisoned tilt. A smart opponent might send in a minion to inflict a tilt like that while waiting, due to their awareness of the gauru form's danger.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, they don't take aggravated from the things that normally cause it. Only silver and supernatural abilities expressly designed to cause aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:15:43-07:00","id":437433,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I believe Gauru does <i>not</i> have inherent armour any more, that's an error on the character sheet that's a hold-over from the previous edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:21:18-07:00","id":437437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf#post437362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Werewolf on Werewolf action (not the sexy kind) - I have two werewolves fighting. One goes to Gauru, then deathrages. This pulls the other into Deathrage. They are now beating on one another. I don't see a 'fox frenzy' anymore, and so do the two just wail on one another until someones Basu-Im timer clicks out, and dies horrifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ape shall not kill ape&quot;, or rather, the People don't kill the People. Werewolves aren't <i>supposed </i>to be killing each other but, when they do, they do so with intent and given the different Harmony rules this means one thing: silver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Werewolf on anything that doesn't do aggravated - I understand that the harrying phase, werewolves actually heal less now than before, but once the Gauru kicks out, things go nuts. My issue here, is if things ever go sour, the werewolf hits the big red button and kills everything. How does an Azlu or beshilu pose a combative threat? Are in oWod with aggravated all day, because nothing else save dropping a building on the werewolf will even slow them down? </div> </div> </div>Azlu's and beshilu's whole schtick is that they don't go head to head with the Foresaken, they split up and run, infect the human infrastructure and wield that to make the lives of the Werewolves difficult. Also: silver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Aggravated: So using silver does the trick. Is the system really pushing for more aggravated to be present? I find that kind of disturbing if its the case, but perhaps I'm still locked in 1.0, where you learn 'aggravated is no no'. I guess the idea of having more things do aggravated kind of unnerves me. In addition, I believe it mentions that werewolves do not take aggravated from anything mundane anymore, only supernatural and silver. Is this the case? I have another question about dealing aggravated, but I'll make a separate topic for it. </div> </div> </div>It does seem that way, but the horror is less about your primary character getting messed up (as that's hard to do) and more about how your wolf-blooded and human <i>packmates</i>can be put at risk by your actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like to run encounters that involve investigation and social antics, and lead up to combats, same as everyone else. I want to make those combats hard pressed and the victory leaving the players thinking DAMN. Reading the book, unless I'm dealing with other Uratha, I get the feeling the end results is Gauru popping noises and switching to Down and Dirty, because, might as well.<br /> <br /> Could I get some help? I've been thinking about this a lot, and can't wrap my brain around it. </div> </div> </div>Depends on who they're fighting, but for the most part Uratha are hunters, predators. Unless they're hunting things like powerful spirits, sorcerers, other werewolves, human institutions, &amp;c, it's not going to be a challenge to fight the thing (though catching or killing can be difficult).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T13:48:02-07:00","id":437483,"title":"","content":"That's great advice, thank you! I appreciate it a lot. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it help to give some combat examples and scenarios? </div> </div> </div> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\">Acrozatarim</a></b><br /> <br /> I'd love to hear some examples and scenarios if you don't mind. I feel that would be a great benefit to the community and myself, having not had a chance to play with the new rules quite yet, and still kind of mind blown by the updates. <br /> <br /> If you are in a sharing mood, I'd love to hear how two uratha were whacked in just as many turns. I'm really against player killing, but know that a playtest is a completely different environment, and the 'how much can they take' has to come up. I'm curious about how much they took. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:07:20-07:00","id":437512,"title":"","content":"Another point to consider is that werewolves in Kuruth have no qualms about devouring another werewolf for Essence. The attack used to consume flesh for Essence does aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Of course if both are in Kuruth then they'll be working together to kill everyone else instead of each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:12:00-07:00","id":437522,"title":"","content":"I picture a battle between two werewolves in the Gauru form to be something like this<br /> <br /> Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham! Wham!<br /> <br /> Once the rage has run out for one, it goes to something like this<br /> <br /> Wham! Ouch! Wham! Ouch! Wham! Ouch! Wham! Ouch!<br /> <br /> I thought of the same thing. If they are in Basu-lm, then this can go on for a long time. Since a round is about 3 seconds 10 minutes may as well be forever. I guess that is when you have to pull out the silver.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to another point. If Silver is an automatic trigger, which will send them into Wasu-lm, and all Wasu-lm eventaully leads to Basu-lm, and Basu-lm spreads, then as soon as the silver bullets start flying than everyone is going to start deathraging eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:14:31-07:00","id":437524,"title":"","content":"All Wasu-Im doesn't necessarily lead to Basu-Im, and Basu-Im only spreads to packmates, but yes. Shooting silver at a werewolf will both hurt and enrage the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:34:44-07:00","id":437542,"title":"","content":"Tried some test scenarios against Gauru. Four fairly well trained mooks with semi-automatic guns can take one down....<br /> <br /> Granted, most of the time they die horrifically, but they often leave 6-7 aggravated damage from roll-over in their wake which is considerable enough for my tastes.<br /> <br /> As was said previous, numbers, tactics and powers can shape the tide of the war form onslaught. Ever faced twenty beshilu? No? Yeah neither did the pack next door and they really weren't prepared for it.<br /> <br /> Another thing to really remember is intent in combat. Most combat aside from the Sacred Hunt will probably be to accomplish something other than murdering the shit out of people. Werewolves are also good at murdering the shit out of people. This is okay. Any combat where someone in the pack walks away with one aggravated damage or more is a bad time because that shit sticks around.<br /> <br /> So if your plan is to run a combat heavy kind of Chronicle, stagger your encounters and hunts, chip away at them and apply tactics that counter the war form. Spirits, Claimed and Hosts should reasonably know what to expect from Uratha, some hunters as well, depending on their flavour of lunacy or hunting methods. Other supernaturals mileage will vary.<br /> <br /> Always remember, anyone can kill a Werewolf with a glock if they roll enough tens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:03:13-07:00","id":437595,"title":"","content":"Don't forget, Gauru werewolves now get their defense vs firearms. Let's do some numbers.<br /> <br /> 4 well trained mooks would probably have about 11 dice to start? (4 dex, 4 firearms, specialty, 3 rd burst, sight of some kind) minus the defense, then multiple attackers.....Gauru has 7 strength, 3 brawl, specialty, ignores skill for defense, has +2 lethal attack against humans. Can't run, so attack 1 per turn with: 11 dice - 4 (lower of dex or wits, advanced mercenaries)= 7 dice, so 2 successes for 4 lethal and grapple to bodyshield it and finish it off with a friends attack. So 1 mook per round for arguments sake, then we'll try with lots of armor and sneaky, so 1 mook every 2 rounds, despite that lunacy would have them pissing themselves. <br /> <br /> Gauru werewolf has 3 stamina, plus 4 health for Gauru so: 12 health levels total<br /> <br /> Mook attack pools:<br /> 5<br /> 6<br /> 7<br /> 8 dice <br /> <br /> Mook hits, assuming they win initiative (with the bonus from basic firearms fighting style) -- turn 1 <br /> 1 hit -- 4 lethal (no armor anymore, typo on sheet)<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> <br /> Take one down..pass it around, 3 mooks on the shelf<br /> <br /> 5 <br /> 6<br /> 7<br /> <br /> 1 hit -- 4 lethal<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> <br /> Take one down..pass it around<br /> <br /> 5<br /> 6<br /> <br /> 1 hit -- 4 lethal<br /> 2 hit -- 5 lethal<br /> <br /> Take one down..you get it.<br /> <br /> 5 <br /> <br /> 1 hit -- 4 lethal<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> Turns:<br /> 1: 19 lethal (7 over, so 7 aggravated, 5 healed)<br /> 2: 14 lethal (9 over, so dead)<br /> 3: 9 lethal (still dead)<br /> 4: 4 lethal (probably not alone if he died on turn 2)<br /> <br /> So lets say the werewolf goes first, grabs one and uses him as a shield:<br /> <br /> so 1 guy out, 1 guy shoots his bud, guy 3 and 4 shoot with a -3 concealment penalty onto the wolf<br /> <br /> guy 1 -- 2 dice<br /> guy 2 -- 3 dice<br /> <br /> 1 hit -- 4 lethal<br /> <br /> I could see this going differently. So yeah, I think with a decent damage weapon and multiple attackers could do it. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:06:45-07:00","id":437597,"title":"","content":"As far as the amount of damage a single source can deal, what sort of effect would be needed to one-shot a werewolf? Like, say, dropping a 747 on him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:09:06-07:00","id":437600,"title":"","content":"I was going to suggest shoving them in a vat of molten metal, T-1000 style, but Berserker's Might and Glory 4+ means that they can laugh off the damage from being immersed in molten lead (at least, until they drop out of Gauru and start haemorrhaging Essence). A pity, too, because that probably would have constituted a Level 4 Extreme Environment.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, lots of gun. Like, more gun than whatever you are thinking of. Theoretically, you could fill the tips of hollow-point bullets with silver if you knew you were hunting werewolves; that'd probably qualify as a &quot;silver&quot; bullet, while costing a <i>lot</i> less (you just need a small bead, rather than a whole bullet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:10:45-07:00","id":437602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437512#post437512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point to consider is that werewolves in Kuruth have no qualms about devouring another werewolf for Essence. The attack used to consume flesh for Essence does aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Of course if both are in Kuruth then they'll be working together to kill everyone else instead of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;They can eat the flesh of <b>wolves and humans</b>. For every point<br /> of damage caused by an Uratha\u2019s bite, they can choose to<br /> ingest the flesh and gain a point of Essence. This is a stark<br /> violation of the Oath of the Moon, and always a Harmony<br /> breaking point toward the spirit. When devouring flesh for<br /> Essence, the Uratha causes aggravated wounds.&quot; Page 100 of the rulebook.<br /> <br /> By my reading of the rules the auto aggravated only applies when your trying to consume humans and wolves for essence, not other Uratha.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:13:44-07:00","id":437607,"title":"","content":"Something that can deal at least 24 points of lethal damage. I honestly have never seen or heard of anything doing that much, other than a really big, really beefed up spirit rolling Power + Finesse and using a weapon (like a giant blade made of wrought metal hunks). Think techno spirit Transformer for this example. <br /> <br /> If its a rank 4 spirit, maybe pull a 12/12 power + Finesse, bump those up to 15's with essence in preparation, throw 30 dice and get the jump on them to ignore defense. Use a shady power to get 8 again (cause Rahu get it for 1st level gift, a rank 4 spirit shouldn't have an issue). <br /> <br /> Shoot, unless you roll really well, that's still only 14 successes. <br /> <br /> 1/3 of 30 = 10, 8 again to re-roll the pool, so 3 more successes, 8 again so roll those, 1 more succ for 14 total. With a 3 damage weapon, it is only 17 lethal, and the werewolf survives. <br /> <br /> Maybe a ton of C4 or a serious bomb? Don't those do their rating automatically as damage, then roll the rating for more damage? That '<i>might' </i>do it. <br /> <br /> If I were the spirit, I'd target the head and try to stun the thing, then hit it again and see what happens. If that doesn't do it, discorporate before he gets your license plate number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:17:55-07:00","id":437611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437597#post437597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the amount of damage a single source can deal, what sort of effect would be needed to one-shot a werewolf? Like, say, dropping a 747 on him?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Vampire swinging around a minibus could probably do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:23:01-07:00","id":437614,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13\">pgolasze13</a></b><br /> <br /> On page 285 it specifically states that werewolves eating one another deal aggravated. I read the same passage you did, and thought it was only against humans and mundane wolves, but looks like its against Uratha as well. Look under the Cannibalism header.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:23:05-07:00","id":437615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437602#post437602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By my reading of the rules the auto aggravated only applies when your trying to consume humans and wolves for essence, not other Uratha.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, page 285 makes it pretty clear that &quot;humans&quot; includes werewolves right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:24:18-07:00","id":437617,"title":"","content":"Hit them with a car.<br /> <br /> A SUV has a weapon bonus of 15, plus one for every 20 miles an hour you're going.<br /> <br /> A Performance SUV from Armory would give you a Handling of 3, and a top speed of 165 MPH.<br /> <br /> That's a +23 weapon bonus; I hope you can drive the thing at that speed. And roll something like 13 successes.<br /> <br /> Or, for real overkill: ramming them with a 747 would have a weapon bonus of something like a +59 weapon bonus. One success lets you kill any Werewolf with less than 28 HL in one shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:26:05-07:00","id":437630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437597#post437597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the amount of damage a single source can deal, what sort of effect would be needed to one-shot a werewolf? Like, say, dropping a 747 on him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly 24 lethal damage in one shot? Hmm... probably nothing short of munitions, even normal explosives don't do that much.<br /> <br /> Massive physical trama... Car wreck rules got eased up on a little so to do 24 in one shot you'd need to get a dump truck going 340 mph, which can't really be done. A five car train doing sixty (20 per car, 100 total size = ~25-30 rolled damage) could do that much if you could get the werewolf infront of it at the right time. Or if you get a size 40 vehicle going around 100-150 miles per hour that could do it too.<br /> <br /> So, actually, yes. Getting a plane to land on a Garou <u>might</u> kill it in one shot. 747 should totally do it but a smaller plane might not do the job.<br /> <br /> Large explosions do automatic damage but you'd need enough to blow a sizable building up to do 24 lethal in one go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:27:31-07:00","id":437641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437615#post437615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, page 285 makes it pretty clear that &quot;humans&quot; includes werewolves right there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> whelp there we go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:31:08-07:00","id":437648,"title":"","content":"And that's just Joe Shmoe werewolf. A Rahu with a chip off his shoulder would need ot be hit with 40 lethal to kill it in one stroke. <br /> <br /> 5 stamina, 4 purity (Rahu gift, add Purity to health), 5 base, 4 Gauru, 18 health levels plus Rage Glory git with 4 Glory (reduce 4 lethal). Double the health for lethal, so 36, plus the 4 negated is 40 health levels. <br /> <br /> These guys are sick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:38:53-07:00","id":437653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437483#post437483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's great advice, thank you! I appreciate it a lot.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\">Acrozatarim</a></b><br /> <br /> I'd love to hear some examples and scenarios if you don't mind. I feel that would be a great benefit to the community and myself, having not had a chance to play with the new rules quite yet, and still kind of mind blown by the updates.<br /> <br /> If you are in a sharing mood, I'd love to hear how two uratha were whacked in just as many turns. I'm really against player killing, but know that a playtest is a completely different environment, and the 'how much can they take' has to come up. I'm curious about how much they took.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just to start with the tale of the two dead Uratha. Turns out it was actually three turns, not two.<br /> <br /> So, the four Forsaken of the pack versus four fairly new Pure. The Pure have something to prove, heard of the new Forsaken pack and came in to try and provoke a fight with them by going for their Locus. Their aim was to steal Essence, have a brawl, hopefully beat up the Forsaken a bit and prove their dominance. The PCs, for their part, have pretty much the same idea but from the other side - they want to wound the Pure and drive them off.<br /> <br /> The actual tactics they went for, though, caused the whole thing to turn into a bloody clusterfuck.<br /> <br /> The Pure characters are slightly more combat-tuned than the PCs - most of them have honed a form (usually Urshul) and their natural weapons, and have slightly more Gifts. The mainline fighter has buffed his Stamina in Gauru form and has some appropriate fighting style dots (the one focused on all-out assaults, iirc). That said, they're also built more on thematics than optimisation so the pack leader, for example, has some stuff around using Urhan a lot for ambushes. The PCs themselves are fairly normal starting characters, with every Auspice apart from an elodoth present.<br /> <br /> How it goes down is that, rather than lots of posturing, choosing targets to spread damage around and generally beat the other side up in a healable fashion, the PCs decide to focus fire and take down the person they believe to be the most dangerous target - the Gauru specialist. Legit thinking, but completely taking a werewolf out of the fight like that - especially someone they know is focused on being the heavy hitter and Gauru-user - generally involves <i>killing</i> them.<br /> <br /> As such, when the battle starts, the Pure initially think it's a regular 'I'm harder than you and I'm going to show it' fight, but the player characters all dogpile one victim, the Gauru specialist. He flicks to Gauru asap, but the sheer volume of damage rolling in from four attackers is too much - especially the Rahu whose 8-again kicks in nicely and, more worryingly, the ambush from the Irraka. The Pure try to shift their own tactics and pile damage on the Irraka, who was already carrying a little bit of Aggravated from an earlier encounter.<br /> <br /> Both sides are lugging various arm and leg wracks at this point from the Urshul form attacks.<br /> <br /> Round 2, both the Gauru specialist and the Irraka get the crap pounded out of them The Irraka flicks to Gauru but it's too slow versus the pile-up of damage he's taking, including a fair amount of Aggravated before he ever hits the killing form; the Gauru specialist just gets severely injured despite the full health-track clearance of Lethal he's had for two turns. The Rahu also flicks to Gauru to help speed the killing.<br /> <br /> Round 3, both the Irraka and the Gauru specialist die.<br /> <br /> After this, both sides have also wounded the survivors of the other enough that more people could well die or be maimed unless (or even if) they all hit the killing form. Both sides realise this has already gone far further than they ever wanted it to, and the Forsaken allow the Pure to recover the body of their dead packmate and retreat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:50:29-07:00","id":437664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437611#post437611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Vampire swinging around a minibus could probably do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would find that so disappointing.<br /> <br /> Unless the werewolf.also had one and they were fencing with 4+ axle vehicles. Then it would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:56:48-07:00","id":437669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437648#post437648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's just Joe Shmoe werewolf. A Rahu with a chip off his shoulder would need ot be hit with 40 lethal to kill it in one stroke.<br /> <br /> 5 stamina, 4 purity (Rahu gift, add Purity to health), 5 base, 4 Gauru, 18 health levels plus Rage Glory git with 4 Glory (reduce 4 lethal). <b>Double the health for lethal</b>, so 36, plus the 4 negated is 40 health levels.<br /> <br /> These guys are sick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Am I missing something??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:58:12-07:00","id":437670,"title":"","content":"Yea, I'm not really seeing a way for normal humans to ever actually pose any sort of real threat to them without having butt loads of silver on-hand or bringing military levels of firepower. I guess if you're throwing like 20 people with automatics at them, sure, they'd eventually go down, but the likely answer is that they'd kill a lot of guys, run away for a bit, then come back and do it again a little bit later. That doesn't seem <i>that</i> far out there so working as intended I guess?<br /> <br /> The answer I'm seeing is throw silver toting hunters, vampires, mages and other supernatural shit at them if you want a real threat of death without needing to throw endless waves of bodies at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:04:20-07:00","id":437676,"title":"","content":"Well damage isn't <u>supposed</u> to scare werewolves. Their horror comes from the stuff that get involved in and in involving people who can't do what they do. Wolf-Bloods and humans can't take 20 lethal damage to the face and come out fine; they probably's can't take 5 and be &quot;fine&quot;. Death Rage is scary because of what one might do while they are in it and out of control. Sure, you might survive but you might ruin your life in doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:05:20-07:00","id":437677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437669#post437669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Am I missing something??</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to do Aggravated to put down a Garou, they don't go down when full on lethal. So, you need to do double their health boxes in lethal to kill them in one go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:06:21-07:00","id":437678,"title":"","content":"And now I know what to avoid in a fight between werewolves where the objective isn't to kill the other pack outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:11:31-07:00","id":437681,"title":"","content":"I would emphasize that going into the Death Rage is a thematic nightmare. Think of it this way, a new werewolf is in a pack fighting the Pure. One hothead decides that he will transform to Gauru and allows himself to fall into The death rage thinking that he will defeat the pure, after all, what could go wrong...<br /> <br /> ...when he wakes up later, naked and covered and blood, what he missed is the part where the Pure transform to wolves and run away immediately, leaving him with his terrified pack mates who try to restrain him and die in the process. He then rampages around town and demolish a bank and a church in the process before running, howling, into the cornfields. A CNN crew is on the way to investigate.<br /> <br /> so much for combat benefits, maybe that is one reason why death rage is discouraged","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:15:08-07:00","id":437683,"title":"","content":"If he raged, likely his packmates raged. So they aren't targeting one another. Alternatively there may be an elodoth. But lets say he raged.<br /> <br /> Either they play it out, or that's when the ST tells them they all wake up in human form, except one of them is missing an arm, and they don't remember what happened.<br /> <br /> So the Pure could be out there, or could be slowly digesting in their bellies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-11-2015, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:19:07-07:00","id":437687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437683#post437683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If he raged, likely his packmates raged.<br /> <br /> Which is when the ST tells them they all wake up in human form, except one of them is missing an arm, and they don't remember what happened.<br /> <br /> So the Pure could be out there, or could be slowly digesting in their bellies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their bellies would be pretty full if that were the case.<br /> <br /> Then again, that could be human meat instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:28:08-07:00","id":437693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437670#post437670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'm not really seeing a way for normal humans to ever actually pose any sort of real threat to them without having butt loads of silver on-hand or bringing military levels of firepower. I guess if you're throwing like 20 people with automatics at them, sure, they'd eventually go down, but the likely answer is that they'd kill a lot of guys, run away for a bit, then come back and do it again a little bit later. That doesn't seem <i>that</i> far out there so working as intended I guess?<br /> <br /> The answer I'm seeing is throw silver toting hunters, vampires, mages and other supernatural shit at them if you want a real threat of death without needing to throw endless waves of bodies at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even twenty guys. Just four gang bangers with shotguns and the Resolve to make with the Werewolf killing despite their friends dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:46:18-07:00","id":437703,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437677#post437677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to do Aggravated to put down a Garou, they don't go down when full on lethal. So, you need to do double their health boxes in lethal to kill them in one go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok I knew that but my brain just stopped <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437670#post437670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I'm not really seeing a way for normal humans to ever actually pose any sort of real threat to them without having butt loads of silver on-hand or bringing military levels of firepower. I guess if you're throwing like 20 people with automatics at them, sure, they'd eventually go down, but the likely answer is that they'd kill a lot of guys, run away for a bit, then come back and do it again a little bit later. That doesn't seem <i>that</i> far out there so working as intended I guess?<br /> <br /> The answer I'm seeing is throw silver toting hunters, vampires, mages and other supernatural shit at them if you want a real threat of death without needing to throw endless waves of bodies at them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437693#post437693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even twenty guys. Just four gang bangers with shotguns and the Resolve to make with the Werewolf killing despite their friends dying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well normal humans should never be trouble for werewolves, even for the ones that are not combat focused. Primal Fear is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 03-11-2015, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:50:08-07:00","id":437708,"title":"","content":"Nuke 'em from orbit. It's the only way to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:53:56-07:00","id":437712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437693#post437693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even twenty guys. Just four gang bangers with shotguns and the Resolve to make with the Werewolf killing despite their friends dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Course, they're probably be dead before they can kill it thanks to Down and Dirty Combat.<br /> <br /> Unless they're PCs, in which case things get more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:58:29-07:00","id":437716,"title":"","content":"And these white room scenarios always neglect things like gifts and powers and and merits and player decision making capability. It always starts with the problem of two characters with no skills or imagination hitting each other until one dies, followed by a loud complaint about how whatever result isn't how they want the game to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-11-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:01:01-07:00","id":437721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437716#post437716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And these white room scenarios always neglect things like gifts and powers and and merits and player decision making capability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do! I think the point of this thought experiment was to test werewolf durability straight up though rather than simulate how an actual fight would go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:06:12-07:00","id":437725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437678#post437678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now I know what to avoid in a fight between werewolves where the objective isn't to kill the other pack outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. My players in the playtest example <i>intended</i>to drive the other pack back in a non-fatal showdown, but what they actually <i>did</i> was rather different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:43:17-07:00","id":437794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437664#post437664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would find that so disappointing.<br /> <br /> Unless the werewolf.also had one and they were fencing with 4+ axle vehicles. Then it would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>4-axel Fencing (Fighting Style, * to *****)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:04:57-07:00","id":437807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437712#post437712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Course, they're probably be dead before they can kill it thanks to Down and Dirty Combat.<br /> <br /> Unless they're PCs, in which case things get more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to be PC's. They just don't have to be 'most humans,' something which in the World of Darkness, isn't too hard of a feat to manage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:42:44-07:00","id":437842,"title":"","content":"@Kaimuund<br /> I'm looking over that math on page 1 Kaimuund and you've missed the auto successes from their weapon bonus, going by GMC tables that's an automatic 1-4 damage per person depending on what weapons they have so assuming they had small SMGs equipped that would be an extra 4 of total damage on the first turn which would be 23 damage (although that wouldn't have killed it I'd rule as an ST that the wolf shat bricks and fled). On top of that since aggravated stays with a werewolf it would only heal the one lethal so it only had one health left.<br /> <br /> With large SMGs that Uratha would be dead on the first turn (27 damage) with those numbers since the large SMGs give a +2L instead of +1L.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 03-11-2015, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:53:11-07:00","id":437872,"title":"","content":"A lot of Gifts that enhance a werewolf's physical abilities activate automatically and for free while Death Raging, too. It's a scary beast, that <i>Kuruth</i>!<br /> <br /> The answer to &quot;How do you kill a werewolf?&quot; is, as you can see, a tricky one. Your best bet is to do so at a distance, using their weaknesses. The thing is, if you're resorting to doing so <i>in melee range, where Gauru can get to you</i>, you're not fighting on your terms. You're going to lose (especially if you're considered weak enough to use the Down and Dirty combat option), because what werewolves in Gauru <i>do </i>is kill you with unrelenting savagery. Whatever plan you came up with has failed, because obviously now you're confronting a werewolf in Gauru up close.<br /> <br /> Bombs, guns, poisons to weaken them, silver, snipers, fire, etc. Basically, anything you can to dictate the terms of the encounter. Slow them down, soften them up. Another problem is that surprise is difficult, at best, given a werewolf's keen senses. Pumping gas into a room or setting their homes on fire (and doing so without them knowing at all that you're there) may not be enough to get them before they detect it and escape somehow.<br /> <br /> Even better is bringing your own supernatural powers to bear, but once again, not in direct conflict. That's how it works now. Werewolves thrive on that. You want to go toe-to-toe with them and they take Gauru form, you're fucked. Unless you can somehow amp yourself up to that level, you likely have little chance of victory, especially with their rapid regeneration. These aren't the days where a Promethean or beefed-up vampire or mage or whatever can just smack a werewolf around. The world's deadliest hunters are well-equipped to hunt the world's deadliest prey.<br /> <br /> Something like a changeling's ability to turn into fire or water, an actual element, or the ability to take Twilight form, etc. Something that will change the terms of battle considerably. Illusions, flight, dematerializing, changing form somehow, or mind control powers. Whatever takes you out of direct battle with Gauru is going to help. It won't necessarily put the werewolf down, but it'll help your chances.<br /> <br /> The final problem is that, more than any other supernatural creature type, werewolves operate in close-knit groups. You may be able to overcome a single werewolf using the above tactics. The real kicker is overcoming an entire pack that way. It's why the things that werewolves hunt are all badass on their own. Old, powerful Azarath are sufficiently deadly that they can stand up to werewolves. Beshilu fight dirty and on their own terms, and often flee the battle because their goal is never to win in a straight fight. Powerful spirits are deadly enough to hang with Gauru, and obviously the most powerful spirits with which you interact (Rank 4 and 5) are capable of doing some pretty staggering things in their own right. The <i>idigam</i> and other werewolves (often the Pure, but not always) also bring similar prowess to the game.<br /> <br /> So I guess this is a long-winded way of saying that if you don't think mooks can reliably kill a werewolf, that's the game working as intended. Even hitting them with cars is not a guarantee (they take lethal from it, even if mortals would take aggravated), and they're resistant to toxins. Their senses are super-sharp, they can access the spirit world and its magic. They are difficult to kill; not as difficult as the werewolves which outright <i>require </i>silver to even legitimately hurt them, but pretty damn close. If you can't find a way to move the battle away from a purely physical one, you're probably going to lose.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are scary, yo. In this edition, they be fuckin' <i>everybody </i>up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 03-11-2015, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:58:57-07:00","id":437875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437872#post437872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even better is bringing your own supernatural powers to bear, but once again, not in direct conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But I want to <i>Force Choke</i> a Gauru to death using Forces 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Guess I'll have to do it while invisible, soundless, scentless (Life 2?), and flying! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT]: I realize there are several fairly obvious counters to this, e.g. a spirit of deception, illusion, or invisibility would be able to pinpoint the mage fairly easily (deception being best since it'd be able to defeat any Prime based magic hiding) and leave them susceptible to attack by packmates or other spirits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 03-11-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T18:59:07-07:00","id":437876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437716#post437716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And these white room scenarios always neglect things like gifts and powers and and merits and player decision making capability. It always starts with the problem of two characters with no skills or imagination hitting each other until one dies, followed by a loud complaint about how whatever result isn't how they want the game to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I have found that when in the heat of the moment, I as a PC always find myself well well below a DM's expectations where lateral thinking is concerned. When you have rp'ers in the moment all bets are off while we dive towards 'a good death' like lemmings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:01:54-07:00","id":437878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437875#post437875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I want to <i>Force Choke</i> a Gauru to death using Forces 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Guess I'll have to do it while invisible, soundless, scentless (Life 2?), and flying! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of mojo working just to kill even one werewolf that way! :P And you'd better hope they have no Gifts that lets them see invisible things or sense you, and you have to take into account the totem.<br /> <br /> And above all that, if you <i>can </i>make yourself reliably invisible, soundless, scentless, and flying, you've probably conquered most physical challenges. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:06:33-07:00","id":437881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437878#post437878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a lot of mojo working just to kill even one werewolf that way! :P And you'd better hope they have no Gifts that lets them see invisible things or sense you, and you have to take into account the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ack, you beat my edit! Yeah, there are totally ways to get around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And above all that, if you <i>can </i>make yourself reliably invisible, soundless, scentless, and flying, you've probably conquered most physical challenges. :P </div> </div> </div>Eh, other than scentless (which I'm pretty sure would be Life 2), the others are all Forces 3 and you'd already need Forces 4 for a lethal damage <i>force choke</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:44:29-07:00","id":437914,"title":"","content":"I think back to an adventure back when we played Apocalypse ( it is worth mentioning because 2nd Ed forsaken is still on th same evolutionary tree as Apocalypse). It was &quot;under a blood red moon&quot; and basically was a city wide war between the werewolves and vampires. What basically happened is that every vampire pulled their silver weapons and ammo out of the cup board and silver bullets were flying all over the city.<br /> <br /> I did some research, about 26,000 tons of silver has been mined out of the ground in the real world so it is available. Sure silver bullets are a novelty, but there are makers. Imagine a world where werewolves really existed, you can bet there would be distributors of silver bullets just in case. Supernatural beings with long memories could entire operations to ensure that that tools would be available just in case the local werewolves got a little rowdy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T20:07:52-07:00","id":437950,"title":"","content":"Another thought I had about werewolf the forsaken in general is that they are trying to balance the 5 forms more. For example, in a city , Dalu would be the form of choice when getting in a fight if there are humans around. This would be something that would be easier to kill rather than always assuming every fight with werewolves leads to death rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:25:08-07:00","id":437993,"title":"","content":"For fun and since I took the Mage side: how would a Werewolf pack kill a Mage Cabal?<br /> <br /> Mages are the one prey I would call a <i>Siskur Dah</i> on. Scaring prey by letting them know they're prey is usually pretty effective, but Mages get exponentially more powerful given any time to prepare at all and something like <i>Siskur Dah</i> would certainly trigger some sort of mystical something that'd tip off a cabal.<br /> <br /> First Priority: I'd hit their Acanthus first, in broad daylight, in the middle of a busy street, and with a spirit of Time sitting there preventing any rewind <i>shenanigans</i>.<br /> <br /> Second Priority: the Mastigos should be taken out the same way as the Acanthus, and as close to the same time as possible. By taking out these two you've severely hampered the most direct means the cabal has of pointing their Obrimos and nuking you from orbit.<br /> <br /> Third Priority: the Thyrsus goes down next, and with as many of the core pack as you can muster. Again, crowds are key, and herding all the spirits out of the area first might be wise depending on how confident you are in preventing the Thyrsus from taking control of them.<br /> <br /> Lowest Priority: the Obrimos and the Moros, separately, obviously, and the same way as the others. Moros with their ability to turn anything to Silver and Obrimos with the two most versatile (and destructive) Arcana are easily the most dangerous in a straight up fight, but without time to prepare are likely to be relatively easy to take down, especially when contending with Paradox.<br /> <br /> And you'd want to do all of this within an hour or two so that the others weren't clued in to what was going on long enough for them to band together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:46:22-07:00","id":438014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437914#post437914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think back to an adventure back when we played Apocalypse ( it is worth mentioning because 2nd Ed forsaken is still on th same evolutionary tree as Apocalypse). It was &quot;under a blood red moon&quot; and basically was a city wide war between the werewolves and vampires. What basically happened is that every vampire pulled their silver weapons and ammo out of the cup board and silver bullets were flying all over the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apoc, that's somewhat understandable but for Forsaken, I can't really see outright war between to the two due to the packs in the protectorate saying &quot;Do what? And let the aftermath fall on our turf?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt but that doesn't mean sticking his dick into a hornet's nest just for the sake of doing so. Same outlook that the Kindred have. Acknowledge each other, give the nod, and keep out of the other's way because he be shady yo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T01:06:56-07:00","id":438171,"title":"","content":"A proper combat Gauru is throwing around 12+ dice on the attack, has 4+ Armor, ignores skill defense, and has armor penetrating attacks. Humans are not supposed to present a meaningful threat unless you are throwing tanks at the pack (and that might be quite cinematic in the right story). Much like the Incredible Hulk, Superman, or Exalted the stories you tell are more about what devastation you may have caused when you lost control, or who you could not save despite all your power.<br /> <br /> That kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T09:12:13-07:00","id":438508,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman\">DoeMan</a></b><br /> <br /> I did incorporate the weapon damage. The to hit is then added to the weapon damage, which I assumed they'd have something like an AK 47, so 3 damage weapons. That's where I got the 19 initial damage. Since that has carry over into aggravated, it means the next turn where 14 was the given amount only needed 5 damage to fill the track, leaving 9 for carry over, and effectively killing the werewolf. I did success trade in, ie. every 3 dice is 1 success, which is of course a hard and fast method, and doesn't take a lot of outliers from 10 again and such into account, like someone rolling 3 dice with a shotgun and ending up with 7 successes. Happens sometimes. But either way, yeah I see where you're at. Big guns, if more than 1 or 2 and not standing around in easy reach, can make short work of a werewolf. I guess doing the math makes me understand it a lot better. <br /> <br /> Regardless, the concept here is to present combative options to a werewolf group that aren't down and dirty, but could give them something of a run for their money. A completely one sided fight is not an enjoyable experience except once in a while when proving a point (hence Down and Dirty Combat), and I like to have about 3 -4 scenes per game, with one being a pure social, one being investigative, and one being a combat, since rolling dice and fighting as a werewolf is one of the great experiences. I was wondering how to set up more common foes, or what foes in general, would pose a threat to a werewolf pack that could become a good scene. <br /> <br /> So far, I've gotten some good answers:<br /> <br /> Well trained humans with armor and equipment who think, or on top of that, separate one werewolf from the group can effectively down a werewolf in 2 or 3 turns. <br /> <br /> A beefed up Azlu that doesn't stand still to get dog piled can create a challenge (try using the Gauntlet Webs to create a thick gauntlet, then make 'trap doors' to jump through here and there, and have the wolves play 'bop the gopher)<br /> <br /> A group of Beshilu, that as soon as they start to lose, scatter. <br /> <br /> Aiming at mortal allies, who can get killed if one of the werewolves deathrages, effectively forcing the pack to run damage control while still trying to fend off their enemies. <br /> <br /> Pure, or other Forsaken, who can drop a werewolf in 2 rounds, killing or immobilizing them (as the days of all lethal, drop seem to be gone now...and lack of fox frenzy seems to imply that fights don't just break up like they used to). These can be border skirmishes, testing strikes, invasions, resource capturing (loci and other things), or just trying to discorporate a pack's totem and then leave to affect morale but not make one of their pack a martyr. <br /> <br /> A big spirit or collage of spirits. With wicked high stats and a couple dangerous powers, spirits are plentiful, reform upon destruction (unless essence drain or whatever. What's that merit, Essence Block? Might be scary against spirits once their pool gets low..). These I could see as a sort of pack, as a leader and minions, a swarm, a group of toughs, or whatever. The possibilities are of course plentiful. <br /> <br /> Then of course the normal recourse. Don't let them fight direct. <br /> <br /> --Use social manipulation to undermine the pack's allies and resources, start rumors in the Hisil about the pack being oathbreakers, or kill one of their human relatives, or burn down their house. Buy up the land their locus is on and build a housing project, because those always turn out nice, or turn their green pasture into a parking lot. I see and use this as a primary source of contention. Whether it be a pack mates 'girlfriend' or human relation, or just some politicians who are being spirit influenced to mess with the packs assets and who aren't themselves bad people. Or the idea that the Forsaken aren't the good guys. That can be a shock. Anyway, I digress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:51:57-07:00","id":438684,"title":"","content":"I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?<br /> <br /> If it was a Prolonged cast lasting a scene (and most spells that do something to alter the body usually are), I could see an Uratha even in War Form having some trouble if the mage could keep their distance. They might not even need to be particularly skilled with, say, Forces. With Life 5, you can cast &quot;Life Force Assault&quot; and deal Aggravated damage by spending one Mana. Without regeneration abilities, I could see things going very badly for the werewolf. Especially if the mage has a couple of friends and/or fairly high-powered guns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-12-2015, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:58:10-07:00","id":438689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=438684#post438684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>With a Clash of Wills, I do not see why not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T13:18:59-07:00","id":438845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437881#post437881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, other than <b>scentless</b> (which I'm pretty sure would be Life 2), the others are all Forces 3 and you'd already need Forces 4 for a lethal damage <i>force choke</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Impossible Spoor </b>would work wonderfully there, even if you are conventionally scentless and invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:26:13-07:00","id":438897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=438689#post438689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?<br /> <br /> If it was a Prolonged cast lasting a scene (and most spells that do something to alter the body usually are), I could see an Uratha even in War Form having some trouble if the mage could keep their distance. They might not even need to be particularly skilled with, say, Forces. With Life 5, you can cast &quot;Life Force Assault&quot; and deal Aggravated damage by spending one Mana. Without regeneration abilities, I could see things going very badly for the werewolf. Especially if the mage has a couple of friends and/or fairly high-powered guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, this will probably fall under the realm of things Mages cannot do. They can't stop you from spending Vitae or Essence, they can't reverse your condition or force the Spirit or Beast inside you out, they will most likely not be able to negate any form of innate supernatural healing from Kindred spending Vitae to Werewolves in Gauru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:31:48-07:00","id":438899,"title":"","content":"Some other supernaturals can take <i>a</i> 2e werewolf in a straight 1v1 fight but with the exception of 3 off the top of my head (who can go the distance right out of the gate) they have to be cheesed (and therefore thematically exceptional of their kind) to get it to work or they fall under rose's example of being out of direct combat reach by their nature (ex: How do you beat up a math meme? Abyssal Intruder from Intruders of the Abyss)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:28:51-07:00","id":439032,"title":"","content":"An Unchained could likely go toe to toe with a Forsaken of similar experience, but then, they have other bigger concerns than whatever pack can do to them save from being the explicit prey to one of their hunts, and even that would be more than likely negated by switching covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:03:58-07:00","id":439056,"title":"","content":"Its tough to say without a second edition but I imagine a Mummy could though neither a Deceived or Arisen would have much reason for open conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:13:35-07:00","id":439164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=438684#post438684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?<br /> <br /> If it was a Prolonged cast lasting a scene (and most spells that do something to alter the body usually are), I could see an Uratha even in War Form having some trouble if the mage could keep their distance. They might not even need to be particularly skilled with, say, Forces. With Life 5, you can cast &quot;Life Force Assault&quot; and deal Aggravated damage by spending one Mana. Without regeneration abilities, I could see things going very badly for the werewolf. Especially if the mage has a couple of friends and/or fairly high-powered guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a Life or Death spell that made all damage the target takes count as resistant damage for the scene. That seems appropriate enough, so any damage they take has to be healed naturally, as a human would, for as long as the spell remains in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:36:25-07:00","id":439185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=438684#post438684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends.<br /> <br /> Is this in a Werewolf game? If so, do you as Storyteller want an antagonist with that capability? If it suits what you want in the game, and you're willing to deal with the ramifications of a certain stripe of enemies having that power, go ahead.<br /> <br /> Is this a Mage game? If so, the actual mechanics of whether it's possible with Awakened magic become relevant, so you'd need to check the Mage line to see whether it's possible to suppress a fundamental part of another supenatural template like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T00:33:27-07:00","id":439556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439185#post439185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a Mage game? If so, the actual mechanics of whether it's possible with Awakened magic become relevant, so you'd need to check the Mage line to see whether it's possible to suppress a fundamental part of another supernatural template like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It usually isn't without extensive Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T02:25:45-07:00","id":439644,"title":"","content":"I think you might be able to suppress it temporarily. I mean, there are gifts that do that. It's removing the ability permanently that's frowned upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T06:53:10-07:00","id":439837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439644#post439644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be able to suppress it temporarily. I mean, there are gifts that do that. It's removing the ability permanently that's frowned upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, pretty much. Stunting healing isn't altering the template. Resistant damage is the mechanic used for damage that can't be healed by supernatural means and mages do have spells that can inflict it, so the precedence is there. So assuming you're using mages with their full capacity those with the cleverness to use such things could make for pretty scary antagonists if you're wanting to make your players sweat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:01:27-07:00","id":439841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=438684#post438684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even sure if this would even be a plausible concept- but could a more powerful and/or skilled Thyrsus mage who is a Master of Life manage to create a spell that could actually <i>suppress</i> a werewolf's natural regeneration abilities?<br /> <br /> If it was a Prolonged cast lasting a scene (and most spells that do something to alter the body usually are), I could see an Uratha even in War Form having some trouble if the mage could keep their distance. They might not even need to be particularly skilled with, say, Forces. With Life 5, you can cast &quot;Life Force Assault&quot; and deal Aggravated damage by spending one Mana. Without regeneration abilities, I could see things going very badly for the werewolf. Especially if the mage has a couple of friends and/or fairly high-powered guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> (Well, okay, yes, but you'd need Life 7 to do it)<br /> <br /> Mages can't affect the internal powers of supernatural creatures. A spiit mage can attempt to Counterspell Gifts (which turns it into a Clash of Wills between werewolf and mage) but werewolves' regeneration, shapeshifting, spiritual senses, honorary rank, ability to Reach and so on are untouchable except for archmages,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:34:42-07:00","id":439903,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are pretty comparable to other combat-specced 2e Supernaturals. The thing that's so jarring is that they are that good without buying specific supernatural powers. This is because it's entirely possible to play Vampire or Demon without any combat at all. Meanwhile, the Hunt means that most if not all WW games will features combat as a cornerstone piece. This means that all players needs a sort of &quot;minimum competency&quot; to be relevant against the big threats. Garou is a crutch that lets them do that and gives even a completely combat illiterate character a tactical decision to make in every combat.<br /> <br /> To give another example, all Demons are perfect liars. This is because they are playing a spy and lying is part of being a spy, and you are unlikely to play a Demon Chronicle that does not somehow involve (a lot of) lying from all players. Making a player sit out or be a hindrance to the Ring in what is a major part of the game just isn't fun.<br /> <br /> Another important thing to note is that unlike most other splats, Werewolves don't have any powers that flat-out nosell nombat. Even most of their social stuff is based around the social maneuvering system, which deliberately (usually) functions on a timescale that makes it impractical in the face of combat. Meanwhile, a Vampire out of the gate can hypothetically start with Protean 3 and Swarm Form, which by itself can make most combat encounters with a Garou meaningless. The Vampire can't win, but neither will the Garou unless it has fire (and if it has fire, why doesn't the vampire have silver?). Demons can just use &quot;Cool Heads Prevail&quot; and shut down all combat. Knockout Punch works if the Garou is alone, which is admittedly a rarity. Even if the Demon decides they absolutely must fight the Garou, they have things like Hellfire, Silver-On-Demand and Echoing Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-13-2015, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:53:35-07:00","id":439913,"title":"","content":"Silver weapons are kinda niche. Setting stuff on fire is something some werewolves can just <i>do</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:55:48-07:00","id":439917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439841#post439841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> (Well, okay, yes, but you'd need Life 7 to do it)<br /> <br /> Mages can't affect the internal powers of supernatural creatures. A spiit mage can attempt to Counterspell Gifts (which turns it into a Clash of Wills between werewolf and mage) but werewolves' regeneration, shapeshifting, spiritual senses, honorary rank, ability to Reach and so on are untouchable except for archmages,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the one hand, yay for a straight answer! (And from a developer, no less) On the other hand, well crap- there goes an idea I thought was pretty clever. However, Ashenrogue's idea of a combined Life &amp; Death spell that makes all damage resistant sounds like a good alternative. As does a Mage with a focus in Spirit who can Counterspell Gifts. It's probably not the same level of &quot;Oh, crap&quot; as the regeneration being suppressed, but it can be done <i>without </i>involving a character who's way too powerful for most PCs to go toe-to-toe with. So that's a far better end result overall, especially since it probably doesn't require hyper-specialization and/or Archmastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:03:13-07:00","id":439920,"title":"","content":"a vampire (like any other being) with silver weapons is dangerous for werewolves like a werewolf with elemental gift (fire) or armed with a flamethrower or similar things is dangerous for vampires.<br /> Btw, hand to hand combat is actually a suicide for a vampire ( a werewolf with the first dot of favorite form gains exceptions success with three success, and the urshul can wrack and disarm your armed hand automatically and I don't wanna talk about the amazing various gifts ...) and a werewolf also keep full defence against bullets.<br /> Celerity and a silver bullter-big gun is the best solution I see at the moment.<br /> But I hate white room. And werewolves hate to hunt alone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:08:23-07:00","id":439924,"title":"","content":"While I'm not a fan of white room scenarios either, it really seems like their tracking powers and ability to be up and about during daytime would make werewolves the winners in a vampiro-werewolf war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:20:48-07:00","id":439949,"title":"","content":"When it comes to killing anything..... LOTS AND LOTS OF FIRE...<br /> Against the Supernatural, it always comes back to Fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Silver works too...</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:22:17-07:00","id":439950,"title":"","content":"One gets the impression that one of the reasons Hellions don't like them is to nerf them slightly in that particular confrontation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:29:59-07:00","id":439956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439917#post439917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the one hand, yay for a straight answer! (And from a developer, no less) On the other hand, well crap- there goes an idea I thought was pretty clever. However, Ashenrogue's idea of a combined Life &amp; Death spell that makes all damage resistant sounds like a good alternative. As does a Mage with a focus in Spirit who can Counterspell Gifts. It's probably not the same level of &quot;Oh, crap&quot; as the regeneration being suppressed, but it can be done <i>without </i>involving a character who's way too powerful for most PCs to go toe-to-toe with. So that's a far better end result overall, especially since it probably doesn't require hyper-specialization and/or Archmastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, it was highly unlikely you could shut it down wholesale before archmastery, which is why I suggested resistant damage as a suitable alternative. That said, you're probably looking at 4 dots in either Life or Death so it isn't something a starting character is going to have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T08:53:13-07:00","id":439977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439950#post439950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One gets the impression that one of the reasons Hellions don't like them is to nerf them slightly in that particular confrontation.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not alone.<br /> <br /> But in the end it only makes travel through the Gauntlet a little harder, so if that's the reason it's not much of a nerf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:43:43-07:00","id":440130,"title":"","content":"Well, Hellions are rare, and tend to be powerful, so I don't think you'd just bump into one on accident. Either they're causing a ruckus, or you're seeking them out, or both because of the first. Right. <br /> <br /> For controlling a werewolf, as a mage per se, I'd focus less on direct damage and more on environmental. In my (albeit limited in scope. I've run a single Mage chronicle...so not much) personal experience, mage attacks work best when enhancing mundane attacks, ie. super bullets, knife that cuts trucks in half, or by making the environment dangerous. With a limited dice pool, and Uratha either getting pretty decent resistances or having to actually hit them with it in which case they get their defense, you're not going to do enough to even slow them down. I see the Resistant Damage being a cool idea, especially if you could use Matter and make bullets do it. That is, bullets you could fire through a Space Window or from a mile away. Otherwise, you're not going to deal enough to slow them down. Our Pack's basic Rahu has 14 Health levels in Gauru form. No way is a mage going to touch that with a spell. <br /> <br /> However, if you make the street into concrete quicksand, make the air so thick they need to swim through it, give them a friction curse, or sick the dead ghosts of their lost loved ones that they killed in deathrage on them, that might have a stronger effect. I also think using Spirit to give yourself a spirit rank, and then commanding small groups of spirits to deal with the Uratha, who they dislike already, could be effective. A couple small rank 2 spirits can still down an Uratha if they dog pile it. Just need to separate it, get the jump on it, or focus fire. <br /> <br /> I feel like one of the previous posters noted this well: A mage who gets into direct conflict needs to get out. A mage needs preparation, planning, and a side door entrance to be effective, and when dealing with Uratha, will probably take advantage of every single possible beneficial opportunity, as Uratha have something of a reputation. <br /> <br /> Could Mind magic control Wolf Blooded? I feel like using loved ones and non-Uratha pack members would be a major way in for a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:18:54-07:00","id":440174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=439917#post439917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the one hand, yay for a straight answer! (And from a developer, no less) On the other hand, well crap- there goes an idea I thought was pretty clever. However, Ashenrogue's idea of a combined Life &amp; Death spell <b>that makes all damage resistant</b> sounds like a good alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no such thing a resistant damage for werewolves, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:21:55-07:00","id":440183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440130#post440130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Mind magic control Wolf Blooded? I feel like using loved ones and non-Uratha pack members would be a major way in for a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind magic works on just about anything that thinks and isn't outright stated to ignore it, spirits included.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440174#post440174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no such thing a resistant damage for werewolves, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there are spells that cause resistant damage, and a spell that makes damage received resistant isn't too far-fetched. So assuming we're talking about actual mages with the full scope of their abilities this is still something that's on the table. It's a nasty little surprise for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-13-2015, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:29:40-07:00","id":440295,"title":"","content":"&quot;Resistant&quot; damage means it can't be healed with the mage brand of magic. Werewolves don't heal like that to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:42:07-07:00","id":440488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440295#post440295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Resistant&quot; damage means it can't be healed with the mage brand of magic. Werewolves don't heal like that to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it specifically can't be healed by 'supernatural means' and must be healed naturally as per a human. But I digress, it's pretty obvious how this particular method would help in the pursuit of trying to kill a werewolf, so lets move on.<br /> <br /> I've not really gotten that deep into Demon, but what all have they got to throw around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-13-2015, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:50:15-07:00","id":440678,"title":"","content":"They can tweak reality to &quot;just happen&quot; to have whatever they need at the time for starters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:31:48-07:00","id":440790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440678#post440678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can tweak reality to &quot;just happen&quot; to have whatever they need at the time for starters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should really give that gameline another shot. There were some initial things that really irked me about it, but those have turned out to just be the new status quo, which I've come to accept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:24:14-07:00","id":440858,"title":"","content":"I'm confused, why would a mage ever bother with a high dot practice conjunctional Life+Death effect when they could just use any Arcana at 4 to cause aggravated damage that the werewolf has no way to deal with?<br /> <br /> Mages are the only supernatural splat in 2e, so far at least, that have easy access to aggravated damage. And if they get enough turns to prep, and a good roll, they can cause enough agg damage to one shot a werewolf pretty easily, since the potency is built in before hand. Incorporating enough Yantras to account for the -6 or -8 dice penalty to get to 7-8 potency is pretty much all they need to do; only need the one success. They'll be risking paradox, but, still.<br /> <br /> (If the Werewolf is in Gauru and getting extra health levels, or has a particularly high Stamina, you might need two such spells, so hopefully the Mage has a buddy with similar mastery of the Arcana, or can cast sympathetically, so that he can get the spell off a few times in a row)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 03-14-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:40:26-07:00","id":440870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440858#post440858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused, why would a mage ever bother with a high dot practice conjunctional Life+Death effect when they could just use any Arcana at 4 to cause aggravated damage that the werewolf has no way to deal with?<br /> <br /> Mages are the only supernatural splat in 2e, so far at least, that have easy access to aggravated damage. And if they get enough turns to prep, and a good roll, they can cause enough agg damage to one shot a werewolf pretty easily, since the potency is built in before hand. Incorporating enough Yantras to account for the -6 or -8 dice penalty to get to 7-8 potency is pretty much all they need to do; only need the one success. They'll be risking paradox, but, still.<br /> <br /> (If the Werewolf is in Gauru and getting extra health levels, or has a particularly high Stamina, you might need two such spells, so hopefully the Mage has a buddy with similar mastery of the Arcana, or can cast sympathetically, so that he can get the spell off a few times in a row)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can't deal agg until 5th dot. Also, with the lack of speed bumps and needless conjunctional requirements said to be in 2e, It could likely be done with Death 4 OR Life 4. That said, even lower proficiency mages have the option to deal agg with abyssal tainting, but the risks for things like that are obvious. Another problem with big multi-Yantra spells is the time they take to cast. You can only incorporate a single yantra per turn into a spell, so chances are unless you're attempting to assassinate an unaware target, you'll have to hold them off until you can give your spell a big enough boost to ensure a kill, and that isn't necessarily going to be easy.<br /> <br /> Long story short, it isn't that easy. And for good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T05:14:02-07:00","id":441228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440858#post440858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are the only supernatural splat in 2e, so far at least, that have easy access to aggravated damage. And if they get enough turns to prep, and a good roll, they can cause enough agg damage to one shot a werewolf pretty easily, since the potency is built in before hand. Incorporating enough Yantras to account for the -6 or -8 dice penalty to get to 7-8 potency is pretty much all they need to do; only need the one success. They'll be risking paradox, but, still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm. No. Werewolves have the easiest access to Aggravated damage. They just need to start eating their enemies. Any bite attack can be turned to Agg, if you are willing to risk a pretty much guaranteed Harmony shift towards Spirit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T05:40:50-07:00","id":441234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=440870#post440870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can't deal agg until 5th dot. Also, with the lack of speed bumps and needless conjunctional requirements said to be in 2e, It could likely be done with Death 4 OR Life 4</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated is 4th dot +1 Mana in 2e. 5th dot is instant death (but likely only against targets without supernatural toughness).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T06:06:50-07:00","id":441242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=441234#post441234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aggravated is 4th dot +1 Mana in 2e. 5th dot is instant death (but likely only against targets without supernatural toughness).</div> </div> </div> </div>!!<br /> Where'd they sneak in that little tidbit? If that's right, it probably would be a bit easier to kill werewolves with straight up agg damage then, rather than waste a turn making it so that normal damage could stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T06:21:40-07:00","id":441245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-o