r":"saibot","date":". 03-14-2015, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:11:56-07:00","id":441330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=441245#post441245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Follow the link at your own peril:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://warosu.org/tg/thread/38484913#p38490581\" target=\"_blank\">https://warosu.org/tg/thread/38484913#p38490581</a></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how applicable they are, Unmaking spells just got a whole lot scarier. I can see why mage society is based around peacefully settling grievances if every master can casually throw around literal instakill spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T12:03:34-07:00","id":441680,"title":"","content":"To the extent white room scenarios are being discussed, it should be noted that one of the greatest advantages that mages possess is the ability to inflict aggravated damage <b><i>at a distance</i></b>, while also maintaining sufficient versatility to effect a quick and safe escape from most situations and plan a more appropriate counterattack at their discretion and with proper preparation.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, any truly<i> wise</i> mage should know better than to engage a rampaging werewolf in melee combat.<br /> <br /> While we are speculating on anti-werewolf combat techniques for mages, I would suggest utilizing simple levitation spells, and at higher levels of Forces, gravity spells. Werewolves may be tough to kill, but there are extremely few circumstances where they can fly. Even a Blood Talon Rahu in<i> basu-im</i> can do little damage if he's floating a few feet in the air. Also, any mage with sufficient levels of Spirit and less than cordial relations with the local werewolf packs should make friends with Helions. Lots and lots of Helions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 03-14-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:10:52-07:00","id":441769,"title":"","content":"Breath of Air might be a useful facet to know if one finds gravity has abandoned them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:46:07-07:00","id":442069,"title":"","content":"Wrt Demon. I see two ways to go...<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2, Strength 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 1, Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Medicine [Just Bruised] 5, Science 1, Occult 1, Brawl [Grapple] 5, Athletics [Spitting] 5, Intimidation [Glory and Terror] 5<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Terrible Form 4, Advanced Form 1, Professional Training [Thug, add Athletics as an Asset Skill] 5<br /> <b>Embeds:</b> Just Bruised, Victory at Any Price, Shift Consequences, Strike First<br /> <b>Exploits:</b><br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Sonic Acuity, Inhuman Strength, Vicegrip<br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Mantle of Fire, Glory and Terror, Acid Spit<br /> <b>Propulsion:</b> Plasma Drive, Urban Fluidity<br /> <b>Processes:</b> Insect Swarm, Wound Healing, Extra Mechanical Limbs<br /> <br /> <b>Traits:</b> Speed 10, Initiative +6, Health Levels 6, Defense 8 (+2 vs Single Target, +3 if two hands free)<br /> <b>Brawl Attack:</b> +0L (+0A in Grapple), 10 Dice, 9-Again<br /> <b>Spit Acid Attack:</b> +0A, 9 Dice, 9-Again<br /> <b>Grapple Checks:</b> 18 Dice, 9-Again<br /> <br /> <b><i>OR</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 3, Resolve 2, Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Medicine [Just Bruised] 5, Science 1, Ocult 1, Firearms [Rivet Gun] 5, Athletics 5, Intimidation [Glory and Terror] 4<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Terrible Form 4, Advanced Form 1, Whatever You Want 5<br /> <b>Embeds:</b> Just Bruised, Victory at Any Price, Merciless Gunman<br /> <b>Exploits:</b> Hellfire<br /> <b>Modifications:</b> Sonic Acuity, Inhuman Reflexes, Fast Combat, Rivet Arms<br /> <b>Technologies:</b> Blind Sense, Glory and Terror<br /> <b>Propulsion:</b> Plasma Drive, Urban Fluidity<br /> <b>Processes:</b> Insect Swarm, Wound Healing, Magnesium Flare<br /> <br /> <b>Traits:</b> Speed 10, Initiative +8, Health Levels 7, Defense 8 (+2 vs Single Target)<br /> <b>Rivet Gun:</b> +3L (+3A with Hellfire), 11 Dice<br /> <br /> With Build one, you go first and trigger Glory and Terror, rendering a non-zero number of Werewolves Insensate and thus unable to contribute to combat. Your goal is to isolate a target. Then you grapple them and murder them with you 18 dice grapple pool and aggravated bite and Mantle of Fire. Victory at Any Cost ensures that your grapple /will/ land. Insect Swarm, Wound Healing and Urban Fluidity are your oh shit buttons.<br /> <br /> Build two is similar. Trigger Insensate vs as many people as possible to isolate a target. Trigger Hellfire and Merciless Gunman on your weapon as you are able. Use Called Shot [Head] and use Victory at Any Price to make sure you land the hit, stunlocking the target. Like the other build, Insect Swarm, Wound Healing and Urban Fluidity are your oh shit buttons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 03-14-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:09:57-07:00","id":442185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=441680#post441680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the extent white room scenarios are being discussed, it should be noted that one of the greatest advantages that mages possess is the ability to inflict aggravated damage <b><i>at a distance</i></b>, while also maintaining sufficient versatility to effect a quick and safe escape from most situations and plan a more appropriate counterattack at their discretion and with proper preparation.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, any truly<i> wise</i> mage should know better than to engage a rampaging werewolf in melee combat.<br /> <br /> While we are speculating on anti-werewolf combat techniques for mages, I would suggest utilizing simple levitation spells, and at higher levels of Forces, gravity spells. Werewolves may be tough to kill, but there are extremely few circumstances where they can fly. Even a Blood Talon Rahu in<i> basu-im</i> can do little damage if he's floating a few feet in the air. Also, any mage with sufficient levels of Spirit and less than cordial relations with the local werewolf packs should make friends with Helions. Lots and lots of Helions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><i>cough</i> 3 pages ahead of you, buddy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=437875#post437875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But I want to <i>Force Choke</i> a Gauru to death using Forces 4 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Guess I'll have to do it while invisible, soundless, scentless (Life 2?), and flying! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT]: I realize there are several fairly obvious counters to this, e.g. a spirit of deception, illusion, or invisibility would be able to pinpoint the mage fairly easily (deception being best since it'd be able to defeat any Prime based magic hiding) and leave them susceptible to attack by packmates or other spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:41:43-07:00","id":442214,"title":"","content":"@ proindrakenzol: I was not suggesting that the mage use flight on himself as a means of attack or evasion, but rather just <i>levitate the werewolf</i> (or use crushing gravity) where he then cannot move or attack the mage (or anyone or anything else), as well as provide an easy target for retaliation in a manner better suited for a physically weak and squishy human mage.. At higher proficiency, such a tactic could be employed as an area of effect against an entire pack for purposes of attack and escape. There would be no need for all the additional and simultaneous Forces, Life and other effects with their incumbent and necessarily high levels of mastery, mana and lucky dice rolling.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I think we would definitely agree that a smart and experienced pack of werewolves should generally snuff the Obrimos mage with due priority, haste and proficiency in any disagreeable encounter or they might have to embarrassingly explain to all their furry werewolf friends how some puny human treated them like harmless and insignificant children's balloons.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:59:45-07:00","id":442222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=442214#post442214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ proindrakenzol: I was not suggesting that the mage use flight on himself as a means of attack or evasion, but rather just <i>levitate the werewolf</i> (or use crushing gravity) where he then cannot move or attack the mage (or anyone or anything else), as well as provide an easy target for retaliation in a manner better suited for a physically weak and squishy human mage.. At higher proficiency, such a tactic could be employed as an area of effect against an entire pack for purposes of attack and escape. There would be no need for all the additional and simultaneous Forces, Life and other effects with their incumbent and necessarily high levels of mastery, mana and lucky dice rolling.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I think we would definitely agree that a smart and experienced pack of werewolves should generally snuff the Obrimos mage with due priority, haste and proficiency in any disagreeable encounter or they might have to embarrassingly explain to all their furry werewolf friends how some puny human treated them like harmless and insignificant children's balloons.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only ability that would cost Mana for an Obrimos would be going scentless and only requires two dots (and two dots of Life is just generally useful for the self-healing anyway). But yeah, mucking about with gravity/making your enemies float would be pretty awesome, but the floating thing would require a contested roll against each target whereas making yourself fly has the same practical effect and requires only a single success on a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T03:38:15-07:00","id":442397,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind if your a pack of werewolves going after a mage is you can now have mortals in your pack. If you manage to learn about Paradox and have some mortals in the know you can just bring them along with you to make casting spells more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T03:53:01-07:00","id":442411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=442397#post442397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind if your a pack of werewolves going after a mage is you can now have mortals in your pack. If you manage to learn about Paradox and have some mortals in the know you can just bring them along with you to make casting spells more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another thing to keep in mind is that mages also like to congregate in groups. Chances are, if you find one mage, there's more lurking around somewhere. More that will without a doubt learn of their friends demise and <i>will</i> be able to trace the murder back to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:41:10-07:00","id":442815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/437362-how-do-you-kill-a-werewolf?p=442397#post442397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to keep in mind if your a pack of werewolves going after a mage is you can now have mortals in your pack. If you manage to learn about Paradox and have some mortals in the know you can just bring them along with you to make casting spells more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that regular mortals, unlike wolf-blooded packmates, are not immune or resistant to Lunacy (or an werewolf in <i>Kuruth</i>). As explicitly stated in the new corebook, human pack members do not generally accompany their werewolf packmates on a hunt. Using such human packmates as paradox magnets would essentially be treating them as little more than expendable cannon fodder, besides the other dangers of excessive paradox effects that could be just as dangerous to werewolves as to the mages, particularly in light of some of the new material and paradox rules that will be included in Mage 2e posted by Dave B.<br /> <br /> Although white room battles scenarios are fun and amusing, I tend to more often look at relations between major templates as a more cooperative effort. Imagine a group of werewolves who have befriended or allied themselves with local mages (or other powerful supernaturals), and the overwhelming mutual benefit for both groups. If such a group of werewolves were then engage in combat with other more belligerent mages, the best strategy would be to bring you own mages to such an encounter. Even one mage who can proficiently counterspell or identify opposing mage targets would be of incalculable value. A smart Alpha uses all resources at his disposal. A few dots in Allies or Contacts is often worth far more than high power stats, combat merits and characters designed for little else besides violence..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}